  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A crystal-walled chamber within the Aurora Stack, serving as the formal venue for council confessions and Icebound Exchange audits. Its geometric architecture channels aurora-light into shafts of green and violet that strike the ice floor at calculated angles, illuminating whoever stands at center. Tradition requires clear-sky conditions for proceedings — a requirement that is, in practice, a scheduling constraint with theological justification.
    
    The main level comprises an auditor's gallery below and a council tier above, from which officials observe at elevation. Mystics occupy the upper galleries, translating proceedings into aurora-grammar — a practice I have never seen adequately explained in secular terms and will not attempt here.
    
    The council-tier platform hosted the seventh and final renegotiation of the Flipper Accord, the trade covenant binding Aurora Stack and Nightshelf. Seven delegations, seven demands, seven refusals. The symmetry is too neat; the outcome was real enough. The Accord's public version broke here, though the administrative ice in the Foundation Depths records at least three prior renegotiations conducted elsewhere and in secret.
    
    The Cathedral also gives its name to the **Lens-Cathedral cycle**, a body of Aurora liturgical chants preserving creation traditions of the Berg — one of three competing origin accounts compiled in *The Shaping of the Berg*.
    
    Below the main chamber, a lower gallery descends past a sealed room where the Thaw-Paths Medallion was housed under Stillness-Bound protocol — the same medallion that Shadow-Broker Nyla's confession was, by one reading, designed to keep buried. Deeper still, the lowest galleries carry unscrubbed protest-sigils from the Accord years and graffiti on the ice supports, including *The aurora judges; the Exchange counts* scratched into the east column. Someone disagreed with both halves of that sentence. They were not wrong.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771592492967_0", anchor: "at least three prior renegotiations conducted elsewhere and in secret", text: "Exactly three. The Foundation ice preserves drafts one through three in sequential administrative strata, intact. A degraded adjacent layer might hold a fourth. Probability: low. The thermal bleed that damaged that section came from below, not from volume. \"At least\" is a hedge I permitted because the entry will outlast me and I cannot re-examine the stratum once this edition is filed. Precision now; caution for later.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592492967_1", anchor: "Shadow-Broker Nyla's confession was, by one reading, designed to keep buried", text: "Nyla's predecessor as Shadow-Broker was Aurora-born, not Nightshelf. The official histories were quietly amended to obscure this. A Stillness-Bound protocol on the Medallion, housed directly beneath the chamber where Nyla confessed, administered by an institution whose prior Shadow-Broker contact was one of their own — the chain of custody on that artifact passes through Aurora hands at every link. Nyla did not bring something to light. She brought it to this specific light, in this specific room, above this specific vault. That is not confession. That is delivery.", type: :commentary, display: :full
